</table>
<hr>
<h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section A: Multiple Choice Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Choose the correct option for each of the following questions.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> An object is placed at a distance of 15 cm in front of a concave mirror of focal length 10 cm. The image formed will be:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Virtual, erect, and magnified</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Real, inverted, and magnified</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Real, inverted, and diminished</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Virtual, erect, and diminished</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q2.</strong> The refractive index of medium A with respect to medium B is 1.5. What is the refractive index of medium B with respect to medium A?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) 1.5</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) 0.67</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) 0.5</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) 2.0</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q3.</strong> A person cannot see objects beyond 2 m distinctly. This defect can be corrected by using a lens of power:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) +0.5 D</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) -0.5 D</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) +0.2 D</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) -0.2 D</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q4.</strong> Which component of white light undergoes the maximum deviation while passing through a triangular glass prism?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Red light</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Yellow light</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Green light</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Violet light</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q5.</strong> If the length of a metallic wire is doubled while keeping its cross-sectional area constant, its resistance will:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Remain unchanged</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Become half</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Become double</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Become four times</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q6.</strong> Two resistors of 6 &Omega; and 12 &Omega; are connected in parallel. Their equivalent resistance is:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) 18 &Omega;</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) 4 &Omega;</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) 2 &Omega;</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) 8 &Omega;</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q7.</strong> An electric iron consumes 1 kW energy when operated at 220 V. The current flowing through the iron is approximately:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) 4.55 A</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) 2.2 A</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) 10 A</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) 0.45 A</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q8.</strong> The magnetic field inside a long straight current-carrying solenoid is:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Zero</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Decreases as we move towards its ends</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Increases as we move towards its ends</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Is uniform at all points</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q9.</strong> According to Fleming's Left-Hand Rule, the middle finger indicates the direction of:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Magnetic Field</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Electric Current</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Motion of Conductor</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Induced Current</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q10.</strong> The phenomenon of electromagnetic induction is the process of:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Charging a body</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Generating magnetic field due to current passing through a coil</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Producing induced current in a coil due to relative motion between a magnet and the coil</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Rotating a coil of an electric motor</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q11.</strong> The SI unit of electrical resistivity is:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) &Omega;</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) &Omega;&middot;m</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) &Omega; / m</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) W&middot;m</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q12.</strong> Twinkling of stars is primarily due to which optical phenomenon?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Atmospheric dispersion</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Atmospheric scattering</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Atmospheric refraction</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Total internal reflection</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q13.</strong> Which color of light scatters the least when light passes through the atmosphere?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Blue</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Violet</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Red</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Green</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q14.</strong> The focal length of a spherical mirror is +20 cm. The mirror is:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Concave mirror</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Convex mirror</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Plane mirror</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Parabolic mirror</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q15.</strong> The commercial unit of electrical energy is kilowatt-hour (kWh). 1 kWh is equal to:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) 3.6 &times; 10<sup>6</sup>  J</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) 3.6 &times; 10<sup>5</sup>  J</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) 10<sup>3</sup>  J</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) 3.6 &times; 10<sup>3</sup>  J</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q16.</strong> In a domestic circuit, the color of the insulation covering on the live wire is usually:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Green</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Black</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Red or Brown</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Blue</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q17.</strong> A soft iron core placed inside a current-carrying solenoid behaves as an electromagnet because:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) It gains permanent magnetism</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) It gets magnetized only as long as current flows</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) It reduces the strength of magnetic field</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) It opposes current flow</li></ul><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section B: Assertion-Reason Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: For each question, select the appropriate option:
(a) Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.
(b) Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion.
(c) Assertion is true but Reason is false.
(d) Assertion is false but Reason is true.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q18.</strong> Assertion (A): The focal length of a convex lens increases when submerged in water.\nReason (R): The refractive index of glass with respect to water is less than that of glass with respect to air.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both (A) and (R) are true but (R) is NOT the correct explanation of (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) (A) is true but (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) (A) is false but (R) is true.</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q19.</strong> Assertion (A): Connectors of electric heaters are made of alloys rather than pure metals.\nReason (R): Alloys generally have higher resistivity and do not oxidize (burn) readily at high temperatures.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both (A) and (R) are true but (R) is NOT the correct explanation of (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) (A) is true but (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) (A) is false but (R) is true.</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q20.</strong> Assertion (A): Magnetic field lines around a current-carrying straight conductor form concentric circles.\nReason (R): The direction of magnetic field lines is given by Fleming's Right-Hand Rule.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both (A) and (R) are true but (R) is NOT the correct explanation of (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) (A) is true but (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) (A) is false but (R) is true.</li></ul><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section C: Very Short Answer Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Answer all questions briefly. Numerical problems must show formula and calculation steps.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q21.</strong> State Snell's Law of refraction. Write its mathematical expression.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q22.</strong> An object 5 cm in height is placed at a distance of 20 cm in front of a convex mirror of radius of curvature 30 cm. Find the position and nature of the image.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q23.</strong> Why does the Sun appear reddish early in the morning and at sunset?</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q24.</strong> Define 1 Dioptre power of a lens. A lens has a power of -2.5 D. State the nature and focal length of this lens.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q25.</strong> Refer to the given series resistor circuit. Calculate the total equivalent resistance and the current drawn from the battery.</div><div style='text-align:center;margin:8px 0;'><img src='data:image/png;base64,' style='max-width:320px;max-height:220px;' alt='Diagram'></div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q26.</strong> State Ohm's Law. Draw the V-I graph for an ohmic conductor.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q27.</strong> What is a solenoid? Mention two methods to increase the strength of the magnetic field produced by a solenoid.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q28.</strong> State Fleming's Left-Hand Rule clearly specifying the parameter represented by each finger.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q29.</strong> What is short-circuiting? Explain how an electric fuse prevents damage to appliances during short-circuiting.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q30.</strong> An electric bulb is rated 220 V and 100 W. Calculate its resistance and the current flowing through it when operated at rated voltage.</div><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section D: Short Answer Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Answer the following questions in detail.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q31.</strong> Draw a neat ray diagram showing refraction of light through a rectangular glass slab. Label the incident ray, refracted ray, emergent ray, angle of incidence, angle of refraction, and angle of emergence.</div><div style='text-align:center;margin:8px 0;'><img src='data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFWM0AAAADUlEQVR4nGNgAAAAAgABSK+kcQAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==' style='max-width:320px;max-height:220px;' alt='Diagram'></div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q32.</strong> A person suffering from Hypermetropia (farsightedness) cannot clearly see objects closer than 75 cm. Calculate the power of the lens required to read a book clearly held at 25 cm.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q33.</strong> For the parallel resistor combination shown, find: (i) Total equivalent resistance of the circuit, (ii) Total current supplied by the source.</div><div style='text-align:center;margin:8px 0;'><img src='data:image/png;base64,' style='max-width:320px;max-height:220px;' alt='Diagram'></div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q34.</strong> Derive the mathematical expression for the equivalent resistance R<sub>p</sub> of three resistors R<sub>1</sub>, R<sub>2</sub>, and R<sub>3</sub> connected in parallel across a voltage source V.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q35.</strong> Describe an experiment with a neat labelled diagram to trace the magnetic field lines around a straight current-carrying wire. State the Right-Hand Thumb Rule.</div><div style='background:#fef08a;color:#854d0e;padding:6px 12px;border-radius:4px;display:inline-block;font-weight:bold;margin:6px 0;'>[IMAGE NEEDED: NCERT Diagram: magnetic field lines, straight conductor, right hand thumb rule]</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q36.</strong> An electric heater of resistance 50 &Omega; is connected to a 220 V power supply for 2 hours daily. Calculate: (i) Energy consumed in kWh in 30 days, (ii) Total cost of electricity if the cost per unit is Rs. 6.00.</div><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section E: Long Answer Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Answer the following comprehensive questions.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q37.</strong> (a) Derive the Lens Formula <span style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.4em;text-align:center;margin:0 2px;"><span style="border-bottom:1px solid #000;display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">1</span><span style="display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">f</span></span> = <span style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.4em;text-align:center;margin:0 2px;"><span style="border-bottom:1px solid #000;display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">1</span><span style="display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">v</span></span> - <span style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.4em;text-align:center;margin:0 2px;"><span style="border-bottom:1px solid #000;display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">1</span><span style="display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">u</span></span> or state the relation using sign convention.
(b) An object of height 4 cm is placed perpendicular to the principal axis of a concave lens of focal length 20 cm. If the distance of the object from the lens is 30 cm, find the position, size, and nature of the image formed. Draw a ray diagram to illustrate.</div><div style='text-align:center;margin:8px 0;'><img src='data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFWM0AAAADUlEQVR4nGNgAAAAAgABSK+kcQAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==' style='max-width:320px;max-height:220px;' alt='Diagram'></div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q38.</strong> (a) Trace the path of a light ray passing through a glass prism. Label the angle of incidence, angle of refraction, angle of emergence, and angle of deviation.
(b) Explain white light dispersion using a glass prism.
(c) How did Isaac Newton prove that white light is composed of seven constituent colors? Draw a diagram showing recombination of spectrum using two identical prisms.</div><div style='text-align:center;margin:8px 0;'><img src='data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFWM0AAAADUlEQVR4nGNgAAAAAgABSK+kcQAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==' style='max-width:320px;max-height:220px;' alt='Diagram'></div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q39.</strong> For the Wheatstone bridge circuit balanced network shown below, answer the following:
(a) Check if the bridge is balanced.
(b) Calculate the total equivalent resistance between terminals A and B.
(c) Determine the current supplied by the battery.</div><div style='text-align:center;margin:8px 0;'><img src='data:image/png;base64,' style='max-width:320px;max-height:220px;' alt='Diagram'></div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q40.</strong> (a) What is electromagnetic induction? State Faraday's laws of electromagnetic induction.
(b) Explain the principle, construction, and working of an AC Generator with a suitable labelled diagram.
(c) What change is needed to convert an AC Generator into a DC Generator?</div><div style='background:#fef08a;color:#854d0e;padding:6px 12px;border-radius:4px;display:inline-block;font-weight:bold;margin:6px 0;'>[IMAGE NEEDED: NCERT Diagram: AC generator, electromagnetic induction, slip rings, armature coil]</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q41.</strong> (a) Draw a neat labelled diagram of the human eye and explain the functions of: (i) Cornea, (ii) Iris, (iii) Ciliary muscles, (iv) Retina.
(b) What is power of accommodation of the eye?
(c) What is presbyopia? Mention its causes and mode of correction.</div><div style='background:#fef08a;color:#854d0e;padding:6px 12px;border-radius:4px;display:inline-block;font-weight:bold;margin:6px 0;'>[IMAGE NEEDED: NCERT Diagram: human eye, cornea, retina, ciliary muscles]</div>
</body>
</html>